            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Marti87114"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made seven of these luscious meals for supper. I used London Broil in four and Chicken Leg Quarters in the rest. Baked in convection oven for one hour fifteen minutes on 375 degrees F. The meat wasn’t quite done on the two we had tonight, so I continued to cook the others for another half-hour to forty-five minutes. They all turned out super tasty!",
            "datePublished": "2018-07-02T02:38:45.787Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lysak89"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Just made this for the first time and my husband and I loved it!\nIt's incredibly easy and tastes great. I added a little more garlic (minced) to the recipe, because we both love garlic. I mixed the butter (melted) with the water and garlic and then poured it over the meat and veggies. Made it in the oven, and the veggies turned out perfect, the meat was a tad overdone, but still good. I'm going to cut the time down to maybe 45-50 minutes next time and see how that goes.\n\nI'm also thinking of trying individual \"dishes\" for ease of eating later. This is really perfect for a No-Dish-Minimal-Cleanup meal. And being able to eat out of your own personal tin foil bowl sounds like a great idea to me! \n\nWill definitely be making this again!",
            "datePublished": "2017-01-20T00:04:40.247Z"
          },
